							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><img src="http://rds.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0Je5m0.Z7pFLAsAuyajzbkF;_ylu=X3oDMTA4NDgyNWN0BHNlYwNwcm9m/SIG=12ubgi6fc/EXP=1169930430/**http%3A//images.comicbookresources.com/solicits/image082002/big/gi_joe_9.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://rds.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0Je5mmKZ7pF6LQAPSmjzbkF;_ylu=X3oDMTA4NDgyNWN0BHNlYwNwcm9m/SIG=12hvlmmm0/EXP=1169930506/**http%3A//www.bsdsoftware.com/images/PC/1AmericanGladiatorsA.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://rds.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0Je5m2oaLpFEAsAW3KjzbkF;_ylu=X3oDMTA4NDgyNWN0BHNlYwNwcm9m/SIG=129hkrnk1/EXP=1169930792/**http%3A//channels.dal.net/wwf_raw/pics/undertaker01.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://rds.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0Je5mX6aLpFVVcAUDWjzbkF;_ylu=X3oDMTA4NDgyNWN0BHNlYwNwcm9m/SIG=130utfann/EXP=1169930874/**http%3A//www.jazzyjefffreshprince.com/images/freshprince-hesthedalbumcover.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://mud.mm-a3.yimg.com/image/2562463185" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://mud.mm-a8.yimg.com/image/4266644620" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br /><img src="http://rds.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0Je5x47arpF0cQAgz6jzbkF;_ylu=X3oDMTA4NDgyNWN0BHNlYwNwcm9m/SIG=13cpqmeqi/EXP=1169931195/**http%3A//images.webmagic.com/klov.com/screens/S/wStreet_Fighter_II&#039;_-_Champion_Edition.png" alt="" border="0" /><br />i know someone posted Street Figher earlier, but fuck.  that was my shit.  i could tear it up with Ryu.<br /><br /><br /><br />when i was younger, i must&#039;ve thought i was invicible.<br />i&#039;d jump down stairs n&#039; off of buildings out of principle.<br />there wasn&#039;t a tree on my block i hadn&#039;t conquerred.<br />not a single path in the woods i hadn&#039;t wandered.<br />i pondered each of life&#039;s obsurdities as they occurred to me.<br />there&#039;s still quite a few that i look back at with uncertainty.<br />but i never questioned which direction my life was headin&#039; in.<br />i just kept climbin&#039; hills so i could ride down on my sled again.<br />and hill after hill it was that thrill that kept me goin&#039;.<br />a kite in the air unaware of where the wind was blowin&#039;.<br /><br />and i told myself to never grow old.  <br />never go slow when you could be runnin&#039; fast.<br />never come in last.  <br />always be the one to laugh in the face of danger.<br />i must&#039;ve been insane or at least stranger than the rest of my peers<br />testin&#039; my fears to make childhood the best of my years<br />my funnest years.  and if i live another hundred years,<br />then at the end of each December, i&#039;ll remember all the fun and fears<br />and the blunders of my wonder years<br /><br />i remember<br />ninja turtles and g.i. joes<br />i remember<br />playin&#039; war in the woods with my bros<br />i remember<br />havin&#039; to go to school when i didn&#039;t want ta&#039;<br />i remember<br />the thirty man code for contra<br />i remember<br />my first skate deck.  it was a channel one<br />and i remember<br />tryin&#039; kickflips for hours til i landed one.<br /><br /></div>
